From: Nura rc4r series <rc4r@nura.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-oneplus-dsc: prefer the 60 Hz mode

The panel offers a 90 Hz and a 60 Hz mode with the same pixel clock;
the refresh rate is selected by the WRITE_CONTROL_DISPLAY byte sent in
prepare (0x30 for 90 Hz, 0x20 for 60 Hz).  90 Hz was the preferred mode,
so the fbdev console and the compositor's first modeset ran at 90 Hz.
On the OnePlus 7 Pro that first 90 Hz modeset showed garbled colours
until the user switched the desktop to 60 Hz.

It also costs a full modeset at every shutdown: when the compositor
exits, the fbdev client restores its own (preferred, 90 Hz) mode, which
takes the DSI host and PHY down, reprograms the PLL and re-initialises
the panel while the system is going down.  Some of those modesets ended
in a silent warm reset by the secure firmware; the last kernel message
was:

  panel-samsung-oneplus-dsc ae94000.dsi.0: initializing panel at 90 Hz (control-display 0x30)

Make 60 Hz the preferred (and first) mode, so the console and the
compositor start in the same mode.  90 Hz stays available.

Pick the control-display byte from the refresh rate of the mode being
set instead of an exact timing match, and fall back to the preferred
60 Hz byte (with a one-time warning) when prepare runs without a CRTC
state, rather than to 90 Hz.
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-oneplus-dsc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-oneplus-dsc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-oneplus-dsc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-samsung-oneplus-dsc.c
@@ -233,32 +233,43 @@
 	struct drm_connector *connector = ctx->connector;
 	struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state;
 
-	/* The validated preferred mode is the safe fallback during early prepare. */
-	if (!connector || !connector->state || !connector->state->crtc)
-		return 0x30;
-
-	crtc_state = connector->state->crtc->state;
-	if (drm_mode_match(&crtc_state->mode,
-			   &samsung_oneplus_dsc_60hz_mode,
-			   DRM_MODE_MATCH_TIMINGS | DRM_MODE_MATCH_CLOCK))
+	/*
+	 * Without a CRTC state the mode being set is unknown; use the
+	 * preferred 60 Hz mode, which is also what fbdev and the compositor
+	 * start with.
+	 */
+	if (!connector || !connector->state || !connector->state->crtc ||
+	    !connector->state->crtc->state) {
+		dev_warn_once(&ctx->dsi->dev,
+			      "no CRTC state at prepare, using 60 Hz panel command\n");
 		return 0x20;
+	}
 
+	crtc_state = connector->state->crtc->state;
 	if (!drm_mode_match(&crtc_state->mode,
+			    &samsung_oneplus_dsc_60hz_mode,
+			    DRM_MODE_MATCH_TIMINGS | DRM_MODE_MATCH_CLOCK) &&
+	    !drm_mode_match(&crtc_state->mode,
 			    &samsung_oneplus_dsc_90hz_mode,
 			    DRM_MODE_MATCH_TIMINGS | DRM_MODE_MATCH_CLOCK))
 		dev_warn(&ctx->dsi->dev,
-			 "unknown mode " DRM_MODE_FMT ", using 90 Hz panel command\n",
+			 "unknown mode " DRM_MODE_FMT ", choosing the panel command by refresh rate\n",
 			 DRM_MODE_ARG(&crtc_state->mode));
 
-	return 0x30;
+	return drm_mode_vrefresh(&crtc_state->mode) <= 60 ? 0x20 : 0x30;
 }
 
 static int samsung_oneplus_dsc_get_modes(struct drm_panel *panel,
 					 struct drm_connector *connector)
 {
+	/*
+	 * 60 Hz is preferred: the console and the compositor's first modeset
+	 * then match, and fbdev restoring its mode when the compositor exits
+	 * is no longer a full 60 -> 90 Hz modeset. 90 Hz stays selectable.
+	 */
 	static const struct drm_display_mode * const modes[] = {
-		&samsung_oneplus_dsc_90hz_mode,
 		&samsung_oneplus_dsc_60hz_mode,
+		&samsung_oneplus_dsc_90hz_mode,
 	};
 	struct samsung_oneplus_dsc *ctx = to_samsung_oneplus_dsc(panel);
 	struct drm_display_mode *mode;
